cleaner-rules-edge_sync-name = Sync data
cleaner-rules-edge_sync-description = Signs you out of Edge Sync and stops sharing favorites, passwords and settings with your other devices until you sign in again.
cleaner-rules-discord_cache-name = Discord Cache
cleaner-rules-discord_cache-description = Cached images, attachments and compiled scripts from Discord.
cleaner-rules-discord_logs-name = Logs and crash reports
cleaner-rules-discord_logs-description = Diagnostic logs and crash reports from the Discord client.
cleaner-rules-discord_cookies-name = Cookies
cleaner-rules-discord_cookies-description = Signs you out of Discord and resets its window preferences.
cleaner-rules-discord_history-name = Browsing history
cleaner-rules-discord_history-description = Session and connection-security data Discord's embedded browser keeps.
cleaner-rules-spotify_cache-name = Spotify Cache
cleaner-rules-spotify_cache-description = Locally cached tracks and artwork. Music re-downloads on next play.
cleaner-rules-steam_cache-name = Steam Web Cache
cleaner-rules-steam_cache-description = Cached HTML/JS for Steam's built-in browser (store, friends, community).
cleaner-rules-steam_shader_cache-name = Shader cache
cleaner-rules-steam_shader_cache-description = Compiled shaders for installed games. Rebuilt the next time each game runs.
cleaner-rules-steam_depot_cache-name = Download leftovers
cleaner-rules-steam_depot_cache-description = Depot chunks kept after an install or update finished.
cleaner-rules-steam_logs-name = Logs and crash dumps
cleaner-rules-steam_logs-description = Client logs and the dumps written when Steam or a game crashed.
cleaner-rules-vscode_cache-name = VS Code Cache
cleaner-rules-vscode_cache-description = GPU, code and CachedData caches. Rebuilt automatically on next launch.
cleaner-rules-vscode_backup-name = Local file history
cleaner-rules-vscode_backup-description = VS Code's own record of earlier versions of files you've edited, shown in the Timeline view. Loses the ability to restore an older version through VS Code -- doesn't touch the files themselves.
cleaner-rules-telegram_cache-name = Telegram Cache
cleaner-rules-telegram_cache-description = Cached photos, videos and documents from Telegram Desktop.
cleaner-rules-slack_cache-name = Slack Cache
cleaner-rules-slack_cache-description = Cached avatars, files and compiled scripts from the Slack desktop app.
cleaner-rules-teams_cache-name = Microsoft Teams Cache
cleaner-rules-teams_cache-description = Cached images, compiled scripts and logs from Teams.
cleaner-rules-zoom_cache-name = Zoom Data & Logs
cleaner-rules-zoom_cache-description = Zoom's cached data and diagnostic logs. Meeting history is untouched.
cleaner-rules-epic_games_cache-name = Epic Games Launcher Cache
cleaner-rules-epic_games_cache-description = The launcher's web cache and store front assets.
cleaner-rules-epic_crash_reports-name = Crash reports
cleaner-rules-epic_crash_reports-description = Reports written when the launcher crashed.
cleaner-rules-riot_client_logs-name = Riot Client Logs
cleaner-rules-riot_client_logs-description = Diagnostic logs from the Riot Client and its games.
cleaner-rules-overwolf_cache-name = Overwolf Cache & Logs
cleaner-rules-overwolf_cache-description = Overwolf's browser cache and app logs.
cleaner-rules-nvidia_shader_cache-name = NVIDIA Shader Cache
cleaner-rules-nvidia_shader_cache-description = Compiled GPU shaders. Rebuilt automatically -- the first launch of each game is slightly slower afterwards.
cleaner-rules-directx_shader_cache-name = DirectX Shader Cache
cleaner-rules-directx_shader_cache-description = Windows' own compiled shader cache. Rebuilt automatically.
cleaner-rules-adobe_media_cache-name = Adobe Media Cache
cleaner-rules-adobe_media_cache-description = Peak files and conformed audio Adobe apps generate while editing. Regenerated on demand, and often very large.
cleaner-rules-jetbrains_caches-name = JetBrains IDE Caches
cleaner-rules-jetbrains_caches-description = Index and local-history caches across every installed JetBrains IDE.
cleaner-rules-npm_cache-name = npm Cache
cleaner-rules-npm_cache-description = npm's package tarball cache (_cacache). Re-downloaded on demand; frequently gigabytes on a dev machine.
cleaner-rules-yarn_cache-name = Yarn Cache
cleaner-rules-yarn_cache-description = Yarn's global package cache. Re-downloaded on demand.
cleaner-rules-pip_cache-name = pip Cache
cleaner-rules-pip_cache-description = Python wheel and HTTP cache. Re-downloaded on demand.
cleaner-rules-nuget_cache-name = NuGet Cache
cleaner-rules-nuget_cache-description = {"."}NET package cache. Restored on demand.
cleaner-rules-gradle_cache-name = Gradle Cache
cleaner-rules-gradle_cache-description = Gradle's downloaded dependency cache. Re-downloaded on the next build.
cleaner-rules-electron_builder_cache-name = electron-builder Cache
cleaner-rules-electron_builder_cache-description = Downloaded Electron binaries and packaging tools. Re-fetched on the next build.
cleaner-rules-vim_history-name = Vim History
cleaner-rules-vim_history-description = Vim's file, command and search history, plus open buffers -- ~/.viminfo.
cleaner-rules-firefox_cookies-name = Cookies
cleaner-rules-firefox_cookies-description = Signs you out of every site that remembered you.
cleaner-rules-firefox_form_history-name = Form history
cleaner-rules-firefox_form_history-description = Text you typed into web forms and search boxes, offered back as suggestions. Saved logins are not touched.
cleaner-rules-firefox_sessions-name = Open tabs and session
cleaner-rules-firefox_sessions-description = Loses the tabs currently open and the ones "restore last session" would bring back.
cleaner-rules-firefox_crash_reports-name = Crash reports
cleaner-rules-firefox_crash_reports-description = Crash dumps and reports Firefox keeps after it has crashed. Only useful when sending one to Mozilla.
cleaner-rules-librewolf_cache-name = Cache
cleaner-rules-librewolf_cache-description = Cached pages, scripts and images. Rebuilt as you browse.
cleaner-rules-waterfox_cache-name = Cache
cleaner-rules-waterfox_cache-description = Cached pages, scripts and images. Rebuilt as you browse.
cleaner-rules-zen_cache-name = Cache
cleaner-rules-zen_cache-description = Cached pages, scripts and images. Rebuilt as you browse.
cleaner-rules-palemoon_cache-name = Cache
cleaner-rules-palemoon_cache-description = Cached pages, scripts and images. Rebuilt as you browse.
cleaner-rules-thunderbird_cache-name = Cache
cleaner-rules-thunderbird_cache-description = Cached remote content and feed data. Your mail, folders and accounts are not touched.
cleaner-rules-opera_cache-name = Opera Cache
cleaner-rules-opera_cache-description = Opera's page and compiled-script cache.
cleaner-rules-vivaldi_cache-name = Vivaldi Cache
cleaner-rules-vivaldi_cache-description = Vivaldi's page and compiled-script cache.
cleaner-rules-firefox_deep_cache-name = Firefox Cache
cleaner-rules-firefox_deep_cache-description = Every Firefox profile's cache2 and startup cache. Profile folder names are randomized, so this matches all of them.
cleaner-rules-memory_dumps-name = Memory Dumps
cleaner-rules-memory_dumps-description = Crash dumps Windows writes after an application or system crash.
cleaner-rules-windows_error_reporting-name = Windows Error Reporting
cleaner-rules-windows_error_reporting-description = Queued and archived crash reports waiting to be sent to Microsoft.
cleaner-rules-windows_update_leftovers-name = Windows Update Leftovers
cleaner-rules-windows_update_leftovers-description = Installer payloads Windows Update already applied and no longer needs. Often several gigabytes.
cleaner-rules-delivery_optimization_cache-name = Delivery Optimization Cache
cleaner-rules-delivery_optimization_cache-description = Update chunks Windows keeps to share with other PCs on the network.
cleaner-rules-windows_prefetch-name = Prefetch
cleaner-rules-windows_prefetch-description = Launch-timing data Windows uses to speed up app startup. Rebuilt over the next few launches, which are marginally slower.
cleaner-rules-windows_font_cache-name = Font Cache
cleaner-rules-windows_font_cache-description = Rendered font atlases. Rebuilt automatically on next sign-in.
cleaner-rules-thumbnail_cache_deep-name = Thumbnail Cache
cleaner-rules-thumbnail_cache_deep-description = Every cached thumbnail database. Windows rebuilds them as you open folders.
cleaner-rules-icon_cache-name = Icon Cache
cleaner-rules-icon_cache-description = Explorer's cached icon atlases. Rebuilt automatically; fixes stale or blank icons as a side effect.
cleaner-rules-windows_temp_internet_files-name = Internet Explorer / WinINet Cache
cleaner-rules-windows_temp_internet_files-description = The legacy WinINet cache still used by Windows components and older installers.
cleaner-rules-internet_explorer_cookies-name = Internet Explorer / WinINet Cookies
cleaner-rules-internet_explorer_cookies-description = Signs you out of anything still using the legacy IE/WinINet cookie store -- some older Windows components do.
cleaner-rules-internet_explorer_history-name = Internet Explorer / WinINet History
cleaner-rules-internet_explorer_history-description = The legacy browsing history list still used by some older Windows components.
cleaner-rules-internet_explorer_logs-name = Internet Explorer Logs
cleaner-rules-internet_explorer_logs-description = A small branding log IE writes. Diagnostic only.
cleaner-rules-windows_cbs_logs-name = Component Store (CBS) Logs
cleaner-rules-windows_cbs_logs-description = Servicing logs from Windows Update and DISM. Diagnostic only.
cleaner-rules-recent_items_jumplists-name = Recent Items & Jump Lists
cleaner-rules-recent_items_jumplists-description = The recently-opened file list Explorer and taskbar jump lists show. Removes traces of which files you opened, not the files. Leaves File Explorer's own jump list alone, since that file is also where Quick Access's pinned folders live, not just recently-opened ones.
cleaner-rules-windows_explorer_mru-name = Explorer Typed Paths & Dialog History
cleaner-rules-windows_explorer_mru-description = Registry traces of folders you typed into Explorer's address bar and files/folders picked in common Open/Save/Browse dialogs. Removes the history list, not any files.
cleaner-rules-windows_explorer_run-name = Explorer Run Dialog History
cleaner-rules-windows_explorer_run-description = Command history from the Win+R Run dialog.
cleaner-rules-windows_userassist-name = Program launch history (UserAssist)
cleaner-rules-windows_userassist-description = Windows’ count of how often and when you started programs, which orders the Start menu’s most-used list. Windows starts a fresh one.
cleaner-rules-windows_regedit_lastkey-name = Registry Editor: last opened key
cleaner-rules-windows_regedit_lastkey-description = The key Registry Editor reopens at the next time you start it. The registry itself is not touched.
cleaner-rules-windows_explorer_shellbags-name = Explorer Shellbags
cleaner-rules-windows_explorer_shellbags-description = Per-folder Explorer window settings (size, position, view mode) Windows keeps for every folder you've ever opened, including deleted ones. Can reveal folder paths that no longer exist on disk.
cleaner-rules-windows_explorer_recent_documents-name = Explorer Recent Documents (Registry)
cleaner-rules-windows_explorer_recent_documents-description = The registry-side list backing the Recent Documents menu. The on-disk jump-list files it mirrors are already covered by Recent Items & Jump Lists, which protects pinned Quick Access folders; this rule only clears the registry list itself.
cleaner-rules-windows_installer_orphans-name = Downloaded Installers (Temp)
cleaner-rules-windows_installer_orphans-description = Setup payloads installers unpack into Temp and leave behind.
cleaner-rules-dns_cache-name = DNS Cache
cleaner-rules-dns_cache-description = Flushes the Windows DNS resolver cache. Nothing to quarantine -- runs ipconfig /flushdns directly.
cleaner-rules-windows_setup_logs-name = Setup logs
cleaner-rules-windows_setup_logs-description = Logs written during Windows installs and feature updates. Kept forever, read once.
cleaner-rules-windows_servicing_logs-name = Update and servicing logs
cleaner-rules-windows_servicing_logs-description = Windows Update and DISM logs. Diagnostic only; Windows writes fresh ones as it goes.
cleaner-rules-windows_system_temp-name = System temp folder
cleaner-rules-windows_system_temp-description = The machine-wide temp folder, as opposed to your own. Anything still in use is skipped.
cleaner-rules-malwarebytes_logs-name = Service logs
cleaner-rules-malwarebytes_logs-description = Scan and service logs. Scan history in the app itself is unaffected.
cleaner-rules-office_web_cache-name = Web and document cache
cleaner-rules-office_web_cache-description = Cached copies of online documents and web content. Re-fetched when reopened.
cleaner-rules-office_mru-name = Recently used documents
cleaner-rules-office_mru-description = The shortcuts Office shows for files you've recently opened. Not the files themselves.
cleaner-rules-qbittorrent_logs-name = Logs
cleaner-rules-qbittorrent_logs-description = Execution log. Torrents, settings and queued downloads are untouched.
cleaner-rules-blitz_cache-name = Cache
cleaner-rules-blitz_cache-description = Cached champion data, images and overlays. Re-downloaded on next launch.
cleaner-rules-ubisoft_connect_cache-name = Cache
cleaner-rules-ubisoft_connect_cache-description = Cached store pages, artwork and news for the launcher.
cleaner-rules-league_of_legends_logs-name = Game logs
cleaner-rules-league_of_legends_logs-description = Per-match client and game logs. Kept indefinitely, read almost never.
cleaner-rules-recycle_bin-name = Recycle Bin
cleaner-rules-recycle_bin-description = Files you have already deleted, still using the space until the bin is emptied. Emptying it is the point, so nothing here comes back on its own.
cleaner-rules-user_temp-name = Temp folder
cleaner-rules-user_temp-description = The scratch folder Windows, installers and half the programs on the machine write into and rarely clean up after themselves.
cleaner-rules-system_empty_space-name = Free disk space
cleaner-rules-system_empty_space-description = Overwrites the free space on a drive you choose (with zeros, or three passes of random data), then deletes the filler, so files you deleted earlier can't be recovered. It can take hours. It frees no space, does nothing useful on an SSD with TRIM, and adds write wear.
cleaner-rules-defender_history-name = Scan history
cleaner-rules-defender_history-description = Stored results of past Defender scans and the log that lists them. Protection is unaffected; Defender starts a new record with its next scan.
cleaner-rules-defender_temp-name = Temporary files
cleaner-rules-defender_temp-description = Update installers and logs Defender leaves behind in Windows' temp and update folders once it has used them.
cleaner-rules-defender_quarantine-name = Quarantined files
cleaner-rules-defender_quarantine-description = Files Defender caught and locked away. Quarantine is how Defender gives back a file it flagged by mistake -- once this is cleared, a false positive can never be restored.
cleaner-rules-defender_backup-name = Definition backup
cleaner-rules-defender_backup-description = The previous set of virus definitions, kept so Defender can roll back a bad update. A new backup arrives with the next update, but until then there is nothing to roll back to.
cleaner-rules-defender_logs-name = Logs
cleaner-rules-defender_logs-description = Defender's own service and diagnostic logs. Only useful when troubleshooting Defender itself; it writes new ones as it runs.
cleaner-rules-winrar_history-name = History
cleaner-rules-winrar_history-description = WinRAR's remembered archive names, extract-to folders and search terms. The archives themselves are not touched.
cleaner-rules-winrar_temp-name = Temporary files
cleaner-rules-winrar_temp-description = Temp files WinRAR left behind in its own program folder. Archives and settings are untouched.
cleaner-rules-paint_recent-name = Recent files
cleaner-rules-paint_recent-description = The list of images Paint recently opened. The images themselves are not touched.
cleaner-rules-wordpad_recent-name = Recent files
cleaner-rules-wordpad_recent-description = The list of documents WordPad recently opened. The documents themselves are not touched.
cleaner-rules-windows_media_player_history-name = Recent files and folders
cleaner-rules-windows_media_player_history-description = The files and web addresses Windows Media Player recently played, and the folders it remembers for Open and Save. The media itself is not touched.
cleaner-rules-windows_media_player_cache-name = Cache
cleaner-rules-windows_media_player_cache-description = Cached album art and transcoded files. Rebuilt the next time you play or sync.
cleaner-rules-winzip_history-name = History
cleaner-rules-winzip_history-description = WinZip’s remembered archive names and jobs. The archives themselves are not touched.
cleaner-rules-tortoisesvn_history-name = History
cleaner-rules-tortoisesvn_history-description = The repository addresses and commit messages TortoiseSVN remembers for its dialogs. Your working copies are not touched.
cleaner-rules-teamviewer_logs-name = Logs
cleaner-rules-teamviewer_logs-description = TeamViewer’s own diagnostic log files. Your settings and saved connections are not touched.
cleaner-rules-teamviewer_history-name = Connection history
cleaner-rules-teamviewer_history-description = The list of computers you recently connected to. The computers stay in your computer list.
cleaner-rules-filezilla_recent_servers-name = Recent servers
cleaner-rules-filezilla_recent_servers-description = The servers FileZilla lists under “Recent servers” in its connect dropdown. Site Manager entries are not touched.
cleaner-rules-deepscan_backup-name = Backup files
cleaner-rules-deepscan_backup-description = Files ending in .bak, or in up to four letters and a tilde (such as notes.txt~), anywhere in your user folder. Editors often leave the only copy of something behind as a backup, so check the preview for anything you want to keep.
cleaner-rules-deepscan_tmp-name = Office temporary files
cleaner-rules-deepscan_tmp-description = Word (~wr and four digits) and PowerPoint (ppt and four digits) working files, anywhere in your user folder. After a crash, one can hold the only copy of unsaved work.
cleaner-rules-deepscan_vim_swap-name = Vim swap files
cleaner-rules-deepscan_vim_swap-description = Vim's .swp, .swo and .swn files, anywhere in your user folder. Vim writes them while you edit, and after a crash they hold the unsaved changes.
cleaner-rules-deepscan_ds_store-name = {"."}DS_Store files
cleaner-rules-deepscan_ds_store-description = Folder-view files that macOS leaves in folders copied from a Mac. Nothing reads them on Windows.
cleaner-rules-deepscan_thumbs_db-name = Thumbs.db files
cleaner-rules-deepscan_thumbs_db-description = Thumbnail caches that older versions of Windows left in picture folders. Explorer builds new ones if it needs them.
